cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Uncertainty-Aware Life-Cycle Modelling for Building Renovation"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hosseini
    given-names: Parisa
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-0168-8912"
version: 3.2.0
date-released: 2026-09-28
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A reproducible Python research demonstrator integrating uncertainty-aware
  renovation life-cycle costing, component renewal, stakeholder-sensitive
  decision support, traceable modular GWP consequences across A-stage, B4
  replacement, B6 operational energy and explicit terminal C1-C4 accounting,
  with D1/D2 reported separately beyond the system boundary. Module
  applicability, provenance and missing-data gates prevent incomplete evidence
  from being mislabeled as complete Whole-Life Carbon.
keywords:
  - building renovation
  - life-cycle costing
  - uncertainty quantification
  - Monte Carlo simulation
  - robust decision support
  - component lifetime
  - life-cycle carbon
  - operational energy
  - environmental data provenance
